BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Codestable) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary: Codestable) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Many retirees want to earn some extra money or keep their minds active after leaving their) Tj T* (careers. Fixed incomes do not always stretch as far as people expect, and a lot of retirees say) Tj T* (they feel bored or disconnected once they stop working. At the same time, there is a large) Tj T* (amount of freelance work available online, including website updates, spreadsheet cleanup and) Tj T* (simple automation. Most retirees who worked in fields like teaching, nursing, retail or office) Tj T* (administration do not have the technical background to do this kind of work. Existing coding) Tj T* (courses are mostly built for students and career changers in their twenties and thirties. They) Tj T* (move quickly, use a lot of jargon and assume the learner is comfortable with technology.) Tj T* (Retirees who try them often give up. We think this is a real problem for a growing group of) Tj T* (people, and we want to help.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Codestable is an app that teaches basic programming through short guided puzzles. Each puzzle) Tj T* (takes about five to ten minutes and teaches one small idea, such as how a list works or how to) Tj T* (repeat an action. The app gives hints at each step and explains mistakes in plain language) Tj T* (rather than technical terms. Users move through levels, and as they progress the puzzles start) Tj T* (to look more like real freelance tasks, for example fixing a broken web page or sorting a) Tj T* (spreadsheet. The idea is that a retiree can start with no experience and, after a few months of) Tj T* (regular use, have enough skill to take small paid jobs. We chose short puzzles because we) Tj T* (believe older learners prefer manageable sessions that fit into a daily routine and give a) Tj T* (quick feeling of success.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are over fifty million Americans aged sixty-five and older, and the number is growing) Tj T* (every year as the population ages. Many of them are comfortable using smartphones and tablets.) Tj T* (If even a small share of these people were interested in learning to code for part-time income,) Tj T* (the market would be very large. We estimate that if just two percent of retirees subscribed to) Tj T* (a product like ours, that would be a significant business. The freelance economy is also) Tj T* (growing, and more companies are comfortable hiring remote workers for small tasks. We believe) Tj T* (these trends together create a good opportunity for Codestable. Our initial focus will be) Tj T* (retirees in our region, who we can reach through community centers, libraries and senior) Tj T* (programs, before expanding nationally.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Codestable will charge a monthly subscription. We are currently thinking of a price of around) Tj T* (twelve dollars per month, with a free trial period so people can try the app before paying. We) Tj T* (may also offer a discounted yearly plan. In the future we could add other revenue sources, such) Tj T* (as connecting graduates with freelance job platforms and taking a small fee, or partnering with) Tj T* (senior centers and retirement communities that could offer Codestable to their members as a) Tj T* (benefit. We have not yet tested these ideas, and we are still working out the right pricing and) Tj T* (how to bring in users at a low cost. Our main goal right now is to prove that retirees will use) Tj T* (the product regularly and find it valuable.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are many coding education products on the market, including large online course platforms) Tj T* (and several popular apps for learning to program. These products are well funded and have many) Tj T* (users. However, they are generally designed for younger people and do not focus on retirees or) Tj T* (on freelance income. Codestable is different because it is built specifically for older adults) Tj T* (from non-technical backgrounds, with a slower pace, plainer language and a goal of helping) Tj T* (users earn money. We think this focus gives us an advantage, although we recognize that a) Tj ET
